Z||000000||Capt Fiero||02-10-2000||08:02 PM||||My car has to go through emissions testing in about a week, I have replaced the Cat, plugs wires, coil cap rotor oil and filter in the past month.  The reason for the concern is that the engine is tired, I would like to know what other people have found works to be a fail safe to getting a car through emmisions.  I.E. methylhydrate in the gas, retard the timming. I do not remember your name but the person that told me that I was turning the distributor shaft the wrong way you were right.  I know have it advanced to just below knock.  I am open to sugestions<BR>Thank You All <BR>David||||reg||11
Z||000001||Phil||02-10-2000||08:04 PM||||Don't know for sure but I've been told that a can of octane  booster does wonders to help you pass.||||reg||1
Z||000002||theogre||02-10-2000||08:19 PM||||My 87 4 cyl has around 150,000 miles on it. It passes just fine. unless they charge for retesting just run it thru and see if it passes before buying/doing anything.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Capt Fiero||02-10-2000||09:30 PM||||Unless they charge for retesting, it is 24$ each time regardless pass or fail, if I fail it is another 24$.  I am going to fill up with Mohawk 94oct alchole. blended gas and see what happens. ||||reg||10
Z||000004||fierospeeder||02-10-2000||11:11 PM||||The first year i passed.  The second year i failed and found the cause to be a stuck EGR valve.  84 fiero 2.5  96,000 miles.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Alex4mula||02-11-2000||10:01 AM||||My 88 Formula has no cat and had valve problems when I took it to emission test. Timing was at 10 deg with 93 Oct gas. It passed. I was really surprised. Here in FL is only $10.||||reg||1
Z||000006||DRH||02-11-2000||10:47 AM||||Capt Fiero, <BR>They don't test where I live so I don't have any personal experience. From postings I've seen here a bad EGR seems to be a common cause for failure. You might want to check it before you go.<P>Good luck, David.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000007||WKDFIRO||02-11-2000||01:45 PM||||The cat on my Fiero had been the original at 100k miles and finally failed a smog on me. I got the cat replaced and went STRAIGHT from the muffler place to the smog shop and had almost no hydrocarbons. (hydrocarbons #s always get me) I have also replace the o2 sensor the day of testing also and passed.<P>Good luck!<BR>||||reg||2
Z||000008||Capt Fiero||02-11-2000||03:10 PM||||Ye Haw, it passed, with flying colours.  carbon monoxide was not even readable, carbon dioxide  could have been 10x and still passed, nox was close 2500ppm allowable I was at 830ppm.  So I still could have been at almost 3x and still passed, this is so cool.  Thank You everyone, that helped me.  I did take the car for a 20min freeway drive right before the test.  Thank You everyone.  Have a great Day David||||reg||10
Z||000009||william_thorniii||02-11-2000||05:12 PM||||Sounds like your requirements are close to Ohios.  Here they are required to complete a visual inspection as well.  Fortunatly for me that mirror doesn't fit under the car, because I passed all testing cat-less although my nox was getting close to the limit.  <P>William T. Thorn, III||||reg||3
Z||000010||Capt Fiero||02-11-2000||05:29 PM||||Here in B.C. we have to go through a visial inspection, to make sure that all the emmisions equip is on the car, and a mirror test to make sure that the cat is there, then they put the car on a dyno, do an idle test then a drive test, you are allowed to sets of numbers for each test if you fail any of the tests you fail them all and must get it repaired then pay for a new test at 24$ each test.  It kinda sucks, but now you understand why I was so parinoid.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000011||fiero56||02-11-2000||06:08 PM||||William,<BR>I was looking over my emmission test report from last year, and they didn't even test levels of NOx, and they never even opened the decklid. Maybe it is different for different counties. Here it is $20 for the testing.||||reg||1
Z||000012||batboy||02-11-2000||09:19 PM||||Emission testing? What's that? Maybe there is an advantage to living in Kansas after all. Sorry, gotta go! Tornado's coming! Gotta herd my Fieros down into the basement!||||reg||1
